/span></label><input name=\"kb_field_1\" id=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_1\" data-label=\"Email\" type=\"email\" placeholder=\"\" value=\"\" data-type=\"email\" class=\"kb-field kb-text-style-field kb-email-field kb-field-1\" data-required=\"yes\"/></div><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-field kb-form-field-2 kb-field-desk-width-100 kb-input-size-standard\"><label for=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_2\">Mobile Number<span class=\"required\">*</span></label><input name=\"kb_field_2\" id=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_2\" data-label=\"Mobile Number\" type=\"tel\" placeholder=\"\" value=\"\" data-type=\"tel\" class=\"kb-field kb-text-style-field kb-tel-field kb-field-2\" data-required=\"yes\"/></div><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-field kb-form-field-3 kb-field-desk-width-100 kb-input-size-standard\"><label for=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_3\">Court to Appear in <span class=\"required\">*</span></label><input name=\"kb_field_3\" id=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_3\" data-label=\"Court to Appear in \" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"\" value=\"\" data-type=\"text\" class=\"kb-field kb-text-style-field kb-text-field kb-field-3\" data-required=\"yes\"/></div><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-field kb-form-field-4 kb-field-desk-width-100 kb-input-size-standard\"><label for=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_4\">Case Related to<span class=\"required\">*</span></label><textarea name=\"kb_field_4\" id=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_4\" data-label=\"Case Related to\" type=\"textarea\" placeholder=\"\" data-type=\"textarea\" class=\"kb-field kb-text-style-field kb-textarea-field kb-field-4\" rows=\"1\" data-required=\"yes\"></textarea></div><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_kb_form_id\" value=\"7744_eacc90-ec\"/><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_kb_form_post_id\" value=\"7744\"/><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"action\" value=\"kb_process_ajax_submit\"/><label class=\"kadence-verify-label\">Email<input class=\"kadence-blocks-field verify\" type=\"text\" name=\"_kb_verify_email\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" aria-hidden=\"true\" placeholder=\"Email\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-1p-ignore=\"true\" data-lpignore=\"true\" /></label><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-field kb-submit-field kb-field-desk-width-100\"><button class=\"kb-forms-submit button kb-button-size-standard kb-button-width-auto\">Connect me with a Attorney</button></div></form></div>\n<noscript><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-message kadence-blocks-form-warning\">Please enable JavaScript in your browser to submit the form</div><style>.kadence-form-7744_eacc90-ec .kadence-blocks-form-field.kb-submit-field { display: none; }</style></noscript></div></div>\n\n</div></div></div></div>\n\n</div></div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>If you are a resident of Lake County or have ever had a legal issue in the area, you may have heard of the Lake County Circuit Court. This court is responsible for handling a variety of legal matters, including criminal cases, civil cases, family law matters, and more. In this article, we will provide a comprehensive guide to the Lake County Circuit Court, including its history, structure, and the types of cases it handles.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>History of the Lake County Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Lake County Circuit Court has a long and rich history, dating back to its establishment in 1843. The court was initially established as a county court, with jurisdiction over all legal matters within the county. Over time, the court's jurisdiction expanded, and it became known as the Lake County Circuit Court.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>In the early years, the court was held in various locations throughout the county, including schools, churches, and other public buildings. In 1895, the first courthouse was built in Waukegan, the county seat of Lake County. This courthouse served the county for over 70 years, until it was replaced by a new courthouse in 1967.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Structure of the Lake County Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Lake County Circuit Court is divided into several divisions, each of which is responsible for handling specific types of cases. The main divisions of the court include:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Criminal Division</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The Criminal Division of the Lake County Circuit Court is responsible for handling all criminal cases filed within the county. This includes felony cases, misdemeanor cases, and traffic cases. The division is also responsible for overseeing the county's drug court program.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Civil Division</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The Civil Division of the Lake County Circuit Court handles all civil cases filed within the county. This includes cases involving contracts, personal injury, property disputes, and more. The division is also responsible for overseeing the county's small claims court.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Family Division</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The Family Division of the Lake County Circuit Court handles all family law matters filed within the county. This includes divorce, child custody, child support, and other related matters.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Juvenile Division</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The Juvenile Division of the Lake County Circuit Court handles all cases involving minors. This includes delinquency cases, abuse and neglect cases, and other related matters.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Types of Cases Handled by the Lake County Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>As previously mentioned, the Lake County Circuit Court is responsible for handling a variety of legal matters. Some of the most common types of cases handled by the court include:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Criminal Cases</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Criminal cases are those in which an individual is accused of committing a crime. These cases can range from minor traffic violations to serious felony offenses. The Lake County Circuit Court is responsible for handling all criminal cases filed within the county.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Civil Cases</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Civil cases are those in which one party is suing another party for damages. These cases can involve a variety of legal issues, including breach of contract, personal injury, property disputes, and more.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Family Law Cases</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Family law cases are those in which legal issues arise within a family. These cases can involve divorce, child custody, child support, and other related matters.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Juvenile Cases</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Juvenile cases are those in which minors are involved. These cases can include delinquency cases, abuse and neglect cases, and other related matters.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Lake County Circuit Court Case Lookup</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>To perform a Lake County Circuit Court case lookup, you can use the court's online case search tool. The case search tool allows you to search for cases by party name, case number, or filing date. Once you've entered your search criteria, you'll be able to view a list of cases that match your search. You can then select a case to view more detailed information, including court dates, case documents, and party information.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>It's important to note that not all court records are available online, and some records may be restricted or confidential. If you're unable to find the information you're looking for online, you may need to contact the court directly to request access to court records or copies of court documents.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Accessing Lake County Public Records</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>In addition to court records, the Lake County Circuit Court also maintains a variety of public records that are available to the public upon request. Public records may include property records, birth and death certificates, marriage licenses, and more.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>To access public records in Lake County, Indiana, you can contact the Lake County Clerk's Office. The Clerk's Office maintains a variety of public records and provides access to those records upon request. You can contact the Clerk's Office at https://lakecountyin.org/clerk/.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you're looking for public records in Lake County, Ohio, you can contact the Lake County Recorder's Office. The Recorder's Office maintains a variety of public records, including property records, and provides access to those records upon request. You can contact the Recorder's Office at https://www.lakecountyohio.gov/recorder/.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>lake county court <strong>schedule</strong> and Zoom Proceedings</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Due to the ongoing COVID-19 pandemic, many court proceedings in Lake County, Indiana and Ohio are being held remotely via Zoom. To access court proceedings via Zoom, you can contact the court directly to obtain information about upcoming court dates and Zoom links.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The Lake County Circuit Court maintains a court schedule on its website that provides information about upcoming court dates and scheduled court proceedings. You can access the court schedule at https://lakecountyin.org/courts/schedules.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Lake County Courts Records Search</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>If you're looking for court records in Lake County, Ohio, you can perform a records search using the Lake County Clerk of Courts website. The website allows you to search for court records by case number, party name, or attorney name. You can access the Clerk of Courts website at https://www.lakecountyohio.gov/clerkofcourts/</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Lake County Circuit Court plays a crucial role in the legal system of Lake County. It is responsible for handling a wide variety of legal matters, from criminal cases to family law matters. Understanding the structure and function of the court can be helpful if you ever find yourself involved in a legal matter in the area.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>FAQs</h2>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>How do I file a case with the Lake County Circuit Court? </strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>You can file a case with the Lake County Circuit Court by visiting the courthouse</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>What are the operating hours of the Lake County Circuit Court? </strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>The Lake County Circuit Court is open from 8:30 am to 5:00 pm, Monday through Friday, except for court holidays.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>How do I find out about the status of my case? </strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>You can check the status of your case by contacting the Clerk of the Circuit Court's office or by accessing the court's online case search tool.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Can I represent myself in court?</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>Yes, you have the right to represent yourself in court, but it is recommended that you seek the advice of an attorney, especially in complex legal matters.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>What should I expect during a court hearing? </strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>During a court hearing, the judge will hear arguments from both sides and make a decision based on the evidence presented. It is important to be respectful and follow the court's rules and procedures.</p>\n",
